# roadmap — Release Milestones & Polyrepo Task Backlog
File: openOODA/roadmap.oot

Ephemeral release milestones, multi-repo progression, and active task backlogs
across the openOODA polyrepo ecosystem. Strategic target architecture is defined in
northstar.oot; mechanical laws in rules.oot; capability contracts in requirements.oot.

## 1. Active Release Milestones

### Milestone 1.0.0 — Ecosystem Convergence & Lowercase Migration
- Canonical Naming: Universal migration of all canonical files (`anchor.oo`, `floor.oo`,
  `rules.oot`, `northstar.oot`, `requirements.oot`, `roadmap.oot`, `building.md`) to lowercase.
- Guidance Demarcation: Strict orthogonal separation of rules, requirements, northstar,
  and roadmap boards ("Less is More"). Elimination of duplicate rules and shadow docs.
- Verification & Clean Ingress/Egress: Update governance scanners and test harnesses to
  enforce fail-closed lowercase verification and `trap ... EXIT` artifact cleanup.
- Double-Run Invariant: Guarantee bit-identical deterministic execution ($Run_1 == Run_2 = 0$)
  across all polyrepo test suites.

## 2. Multi-Repo Release Progression

### Phase 1 — Substrate & Compiler Hardening
- `oodar`: Maintain zero-heap host runtime, seccomp-bpf/Landlock sandbox, 26 capability
  tokens, and zero-heap crash flight sensor.
- `oodac`: Compiler pipeline maturity, Merkle AST caching, SSA optimizations, direct LLVM
  IR emission, and self-hosted bootstrapping towards full parity.

### Phase 2 — Standard Library & Driver Integration
- `std`: Stabilization across all 8 functional domains (`core`, `fs`, `net`, `sec`,
  `science`, `app`, `hw`, `meta`), zero-heap operations, and <= 256 lines per module.
- `cli`: Language CLI driver (`build`, `run`, `test`, `fmt`, `install`, `update`,
  `upgrade`, `init`, `qa`, `context`, `fix`), stationary workspace execution
  ($\Delta_{\text{path}} = 0$). Replaces the language surface of the legacy `ooda/`
  binary.
- `ooda`: Back-compat router that forwards to `cli`, `opm`, `lsp`, `mcp`. Owns
  `spawn.oo` (the spawn dispatcher) and `find_compiler.oo`. Does no in-process
  driver work itself.

### Phase 3 — Operational Logistics & Tooling
- `bb`: Telemetry ring buffer, zero-allocation crash signal interception,
  1-turn autopsy diagnosis, and semantic AST diffing.
- `lsp`: JSON-RPC 2.0 language server daemon, hover, completions, and capability inspection.
- `mcp`: Model Context Protocol tool dispatch, AST slicing, and dynamic capability attenuation.
- `opm`: Cryptographic package manager, minisign verification, and dependency lockfiles.
- `catalog`: Verified public package registry index and capability audit proofs.

### Phase 4 — Delivery, Packaging & Governance
- `install`: Multi-platform machine landing (`install.sh`, apt, dnf, pacman), pre-flight
  checks, fail-closed SHA-256 sidecars, and idempotent dry-run execution.
- `website`: Ecosystem developer portal, interactive simulations, and documentation viewer.
- `openOODA`: Governance hub, RFC lifecycle management, and automated release gates.

